{
  "slug": "artist:earl-sweatshirt",
  "name": "Earl Sweatshirt",
  "editorial_article": "Born Thebe Neruda Kgositsile in Chicago in 1994, Earl Sweatshirt began his career in 2008 as Sly Tendencies before Tyler, the Creator recruited him into the alternative hip-hop collective Odd Future in 2009. His debut mixtape Earl, released in 2010, drew critical acclaim for its horrorcore influence and dense lyricism, shortly preceding his year-and-a-half stay at a therapeutic boarding school in Samoa. Returning to Los Angeles in 2012, he shifted toward abstract and jazz rap, later collaborating with producer The Alchemist on the joint project Voir Dire. His 2018 album Some Rap Songs, which explored themes regarding his late father, poet Keorapetse Kgositsile, adopted a lo-fi, loop-driven production style influenced by the New York underground collective sLUms and rapper Mike. He has consistently utilized the production alias randomblackdude, contributing to his own critically acclaimed releases such as Doris and I Don't Like Shit, I Don't Go Outside.",
